scion: a cache of translated code shared by the JITs of a process (backend/x64/a64_code_cache.cpp): a block one JIT
(guest thread) has compiled is copied into another's code and relocated instead of being compiled again, as long as
the guest instructions there are the same. Needs patches/xbyak-reloc-hook.patch.
- after a block is emitted, the fields that refer outside it are recorded symbolically: rel32 and rip-relative
  references to prelude code, constants, fastmem fallbacks and the host executable, and mov immediates that are the
  JIT's own pointers (configuration, callbacks, tpidr registers, exclusive monitor slots); block links are emitted
  again by the JIT that installs the copy, fastmem fault information is relocated with it
- UserConfig::code_cache (MakeCodeCache), with code_cache_verify (also decode each block with Zydis and compare, and
  compile cached blocks again and compare) and code_cache_selftest (run every block from a relocated copy) for testing

